WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.382
Practice 1 reshapes student grades.

00:00:02.382 --> 00:00:06.312
The source is long: one student-course grade per row.

00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:10.272
The output should have one row per student and fixed course columns.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:16.047
A missing course should remain NULL because no recorded grade is not the same as a grade of zero.

00:00:16.047 --> 00:00:19.552
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.157
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:27.272
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:27.272 --> 00:00:30.652
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:30.652 --> 00:00:36.587
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:42.022
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:44.015
not only whether the statement executes.
